\n'protocol_ref':r['required_study_protocol_ref'],\n'evidence_refs':['baseline-din','g0-r0003-relation_content_counts','g0-r0004-joint_feedback_counts','g0-r0004-zero_feedback_counts','g0-r0006-within_centered','g0-r0006-occupancy_timing','g0-r0010-feedback_bound','g0-r0012-event_silu','g0-r0013-pair_joint_both','g0-r0013-pair_joint_counts','g0-r0016-pair_rank_joint','g0-r0016-pair_rank_marginal','g0-r0016-pair_rank_copy','g0-r0016-pair_rank_zero','g0-r0017-pair_rank_within','g0-r0017-pair_rank_occupancy','g0-r0017-pair_rank_full_replay'],\n'question':'After retaining exact conjunctive content and counts, must a representation unit encode the temporal placement of the conjunction itself, or is placement of the two constituent field relations sufficient?',\n'hypothesis':'The occupancy result suggests that coarse placement, rather than within-conjunction content-order covariance, carries the recent pair-rank gain. A symmetric mean of the two marginal-relation centroids may retain most of that gain when multiplying the SAME true conjunctive content. This is a prospective lower-order representation replacement, not a claim that it already improves quality or has lower measured cost. The competing hypothesis is that conjunction-specific placement is essential.',\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived primary text lines271-283 verifies unnormalized target activation pooling. Retain that inherited component; replace only an existing conjunctive-placement source, not DIN attention normalization. No claim of exact original DIN reproduction.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:HiFormer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark forward/tokenizer lines113-159 pools history with target attention, tokenizes fields/tasks and applies interaction. Inherited local model similarly combines static/history tokens, but the proposed contrast is pair versus marginal rank-centroid binding before its existing interaction block. Benchmark code is not an original-author method audit.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:HyFormer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark block lines221-243 repeatedly encodes sequences, decodes global queries and boosts field/global tokens. No such architecture is newly added here; only an existing fixed summary source changes. Original paper detailed text is unavailable through the authorized registry.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:MixFormer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark block lines187-197 mixes non-sequential queries, retrieves through cross attention and fuses per layer. This experiment preserves the inherited fixed summary and one-block interaction instead of adopting repeated evolving queries.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:dmr','verification':'read','difference':'Only author README lines1-9 is available; it explicitly warns that its histories contain category/brand/behavior and no item. Current adapter exposes previous advertisement fields. No DMR paper-mechanism equivalence or transfer claim is supported.'}],\n'inherited_components':['Complete incumbent g0-r0017-pair_rank_occupancy model and its same 33,130,405 nominal parameters, including 31,793,216 embedding parameters','Six item-field embeddings plus historical action; user/context fields; target action forced zero; masked padded history sanitized before embedding','Unnormalized DIN local activation; global and four valid-rank-quartile summaries; seven target-match relation tokens per temporal bin','Full single-relation moments, duplicate moment residual, relation-specific moment/content banks, factorized feedback-content bank and collapsed joint-feedback memory','Exact 15 pair content/count maps and occupancy pair-rank bank; unchanged pair-to-relation routes, static bypass and all four towers','Host-owned training, split, labels, scoring and all cost accounting'],\n'proposed_difference':'Replace only mu_rs in the exist